            cm_debrief: `Your purchasing plan for Revinuesa: offers are compared on the total cost of acquisition —price, transport, the stock each lead time and its variation force, the orders, the defects and the stops—, not on the price of a bottle; the volume is split between a main supplier and a qualified backup, without cutting it so thin that everyone charges the small-customer price; the contract buys reliability as well as price, without tying the brewery to volumes the plan may not need; what arrives is checked by sampling; invoices are matched with the order and the delivery note before paying within the legal term; suppliers are followed with data; and an alternative already qualified gives supply and negotiating power when the main supplier fails. The cheapest supplier can turn out dear through lead time and reliability.`,
